    "listener_verdict": "The hook was solid\u2014calling out the H100 idling immediately grabbed me because everyone knows those things are expensive paperweights if you don't optimize your kernels. I liked the 'starving for the next token' line. My only gripe is that 'async kernel overlap' is a bit of a buzzword salad if you don't explain that it's basically just hiding memory latency by overlapping data movement with compute cycles. Once you hit Beat 4, it clicked, but Beat 3 felt like you were just throwing jargon at me."
